<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goulfey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goulfey is a town in the Far North Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, near the Chari River and the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, on the plains south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>. It was one of the walled Kotoko towns that had become small kingdoms by the 16th century, paying tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a>, and its sultan remains a traditional ruler.</p></div>
